					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:300px;"><img src="https://artbreeder.b-cdn.net/imgs/d6e55b67e72f39fb7f71.jpeg" style="width:300px;" alt="d6e55b67e72f39fb7f71.jpeg" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:300px;"> <p>The clearest image available of SCP-5422</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5422</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5422 is currently contained by tracking its movement with the use of Foundation satellites. A method of permanent containment is currently undergoing research.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5422 is a UFO of unknown variety or origin. It appears to be a large bubble, measuring roughly 2 meters in length. It is highly mobile, though it never strays from an altitude of approximately 1&#160;km. It moves at a speed of approximately 80&#160;km/h, though this is not constant and it can gradually alter its speed and direction. SCP-5422 always moves towards the nearest cloud. Darker clouds are always chosen over lighter ones, and as such, it typically is found in rain.</p> <p>There appears to be a dark object resting inside of SCP-5422. It is hypothesized to be the source of SCP-5422’s locomotion. However, its function and origin are also unknown.</p> <p>SCP-5422 is believed to have been first spotted as early as 1971. It came to the Foundation’s attention in 2011, after repeated reports of a bubble-like UFO were followed up on. Due to the overwhelming number of false UFO claims from civilians, the use of amnestic treatment for witnesses was not deemed necessary.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;REVISION&nbsp;10/06/11</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5422</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Neutralized</p> <p><strong>Incident Report:</strong> On October 4th, 2011, an attempt to permanently contain SCP-5422 was made. Foundation operatives pinpointed the location of SCP-5422 and moved in to capture it with the use of aircraft. Shortly after, SCP-5422 ruptured from below and released the previously mentioned dark object from within. Attempts to catch the object were unsuccessful. The subsequent search for the object in the Pacific Ocean was unsuccessful. After releasing its contents, SCP-5422 slowed to a stop and floated in place. It was retrieved for study and is now held in storage.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5422 is a deflated uterus of extrasolar origin. Its biological components have been analyzed and traced back to the planet XC-196-H5 in the Andromeda galaxy, which vanished at an indeterminate time between 1957 and 1962. The planet is believed to have entered an unstable orbit, which caused it to exit its solar system. SCP-5422 is believed to have originated from an intelligent organism alive on XC-196-H5 prior to its orbital instability.</p> <p>In addition to its biological components, SCP-5422 has been augmented with technological components, including a small computer. The computer is programmed to locomote SCP-5422 into specific weather and thermal conditions, presumably to aid the growth of the child.</p> <p>The precise method by which SCP-5422 became present on Earth is still unknown. However, it is known that the intelligent life on XC-196-H5 possessed more advanced technological capabilities compared to that of an average human, and it is thus hypothesized that SCP-5422 was sent by a form of teleportation.</p> <p>The ongoing search for the fetus that was once present inside of SCP-5422 remains unsuccessful.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Show&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:300px;"><img src="https://artbreeder.b-cdn.net/imgs/4b81ad1d3d1468c67344.jpeg" style="width:300px;" alt="4b81ad1d3d1468c67344.jpeg" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:300px;"> <p>SCP-5422 after its rupture.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lilac-snow" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5210371&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606746163" alt="Lilac Snow" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5210371)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lilac-snow" >Lilac Snow</a></span></p> 
